# Help people start a household task

Use a start page when preparation, prerequisites or consequences help people begin a task. Put what they need to know above the start button. Do not put a start page in front of a small, reversible preference. Show that preference directly.

These examples are local previews. They do not inspect an installation, add an integration, set up Energy or send notifications.

## Put the essentials before the start button

Say what will be set up, what information or permission it needs, and whether anything switches on straight away. Keep the detail short. Nobody should have to start a wizard to learn that it needs an integration they lack or administrator access.

<%= example('nhs-start-notifications') %>

## Explain a missing prerequisite

If setup is not possible, say what is missing and give a route to fix it. Never leave a disabled “Start now” button without a reason. Do not invent a sensor, imply an integration supplies a measurement it does not, or present a power sensor as an energy total.

<%= example('nhs-start-requirement') %>

## Recognise people who return

If a draft exists, offer to resume it and show enough to recognise it. A saved draft is not an enabled automation. Starting again must not silently discard earlier work or create a duplicate rule.

<%= example('nhs-start-resume') %>

## Keep it accessible

Use the household task as the main heading. Keep required information above the start button and optional detail in short sections or a details control. Do not promise how long setup takes when it depends on device discovery or on the person’s needs. Keep the normal navigation.

An alternative route must exist in this installation. If the only route is native Home Assistant configuration, say so and link to it using a verified Home Assistant path.

## Respect Home Assistant behaviour

Starting a journey opens its first question. It must not send a device command. Check access and capabilities before showing an administrative task. Keep setting up separate from switching on, and use a named final action where switching on matters.

A real start page must match the installed Home Assistant version and stay understandable when an integration is unavailable.

## Choose a nearby pattern when it fits better

Use a [hub](hub.html) to help people find the right task. Use [Complete multiple household tasks](complete-multiple-tasks.html) to resume longer work after it begins. Use [Ask clear questions on pages and in dialogs](question-pages.html) for the questions themselves.
